WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.509
On the Stride, the plan sets the belt speed and the incline.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.191
Set up your run: HIIT intervals, or Steady, one speed and one incline held the whole

00:00:13.191 --> 00:00:13.738
run.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.743
Minute on is six rounds: work at thirteen kilometres an hour on a two percent

00:00:22.743 --> 00:00:24.521
incline, recover at six.

00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:26.460
Each speed shows its pace.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.745
Your run adds it up: sixteen minutes, about two point three five kilometres and

00:00:34.745 --> 00:00:36.727
thirty-five metres of climb.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.713
Steady starts on Hill walk: six and a half, at eight percent.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.602
Clip in the safety key and tap Start run.

00:00:50.802 --> 00:00:53.878
Stand on the side rails: the belt starts in three.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.260
Mid-run, speed reads nine kilometres an hour, six forty a kilometre, at target.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.078
The trace draws speed against the plan, with the incline below.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.484
Take over with Slower and Faster, a quick speed, or the incline bars.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.543
Tap twelve. The belt ramps up, and the plan takes over again next interval.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.427
On a phone, the controls follow the run.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.641
What the tests prove: the belt starts only after a three, two, one countdown.

00:01:42.841 --> 00:01:46.319
And if the Stride stays off for ninety seconds, the run ends.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.090
That is journey six. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live training

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:55.875
display.
